window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-e846a00e03e90691"]={"key":"ny_b1-e846a00e03e90691","group":"ny_b1","uid":"e846a00e03e90691","rank":31,"title":"quillstone dual jurisdiction delivery annex","occupation":"audio_video_technicians","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You are the senior post-production technician at Quillstone Post. Esperanza Beaulieu has promised Orrindale Partners that the co-produced series can go out as one universal master, but we now have a US broadcaster and a European streamer whose delivery expectations do not line up, and business affairs needs the annex before the distribution agreement is signed on the 29th. Please prepare `quillstone_delivery_annex.pdf` in the top level of the working directory. It must contain the technical delivery specification annex and a conformance record for one reference master, written so a regulator, auditor, or compliance reviewer can trace every provision to the standard or contractual basis behind it. Compare the previous draft assumptions with the changed dual-territory requirements and call out material changes. The loudness issue is not theoretical: A/85 points to -24 LKFS while R128 uses -23 LUFS with a -1 dBTP ceiling, and the loudness, true-peak, dialogue-gating, and stem requirements affect one another. Ana Clarkson also wants the rare but serious case of a safety or legal hold after approval addressed separately from normal delivery. Keep the annex operational rather than promotional, do not invent programme facts or contractual figures, and make the final PDF no more than six pages.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `quillstone_delivery_annex.pdf` — A concise technical delivery specification annex containing a conformance record for one reference master. (Write the annex and conformance record as one coherent PDF.; Keep the total document to no more than six pages.; Make the contractual deliverable position explicit rather than using a vague universal broadcast-standard statement.; Trace each substantive provision to an applicable standard, contract requirement, or clearly identified house requirement.; Distinguish normal delivery from the rare safety or legal-hold exception.; Do not invent unsupported programme facts, contractual figures, or completed measurements.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/quillstone_delivery_annex.pdf","bytes":21017,"extension":".pdf","url":"assets/c2ee2053169d9de04e279bdc1c1358ee040184459da963b74c78428a9d819014.pdf","sha256":"c2ee2053169d9de04e279bdc1c1358ee040184459da963b74c78428a9d819014","preview":{"kind":"pdf","text":"QUILLSTONE POST | DELIVERY ANNEX                                                                                                Controlled draft - v1.0 - 20 Aug 2026\n\n\n\n\n                     Technical Delivery Specification Annex\n Quillstone Post / Orrindale Partners co-produced series\n\n Purpose. This annex is the operational delivery position for the first dual-territory package. It is written for business affairs, a\n broadcaster/streamer operations desk, and an external compliance reviewer. It does not certify a media file that was not supplied.\n Contractual deliverable decision (authoritative). The US A/85 master is the contractual reference master for approval,\n archive, and change control. The European streamer receives a controlled R128 derivative made from that approved\n picture and source stems. The derivative is not a second creative approval and cannot replace the reference master. If\n the executed distribution agreement states a different hierarchy, Business Affairs must issue a written change notice\n before mastering.\n\n 1. Scope and jurisdiction map\n   Recipient / use                           Governing delivery position                                                          Status in this annex\n\n   US broadcaster (primary approval)         A/85 loudness regime: -24 LKFS programme target. True-peak and file-format           Authoritative reference master;\n                                             values are recipient-manual items until confirmed.                                   approval gate applies.\n\n   European streamer (controlled             R128 regime: -23 LUFS integrated target and -1 dBTP maximum true peak.               Derivative of approved reference;\n   derivative)                               Confirm any tolerance, channel layout, and platform-specific wrapper rules.          separate QC record.\n\n\n\n Boundary. “Universal master” is retained only as a creative source concept. It is not a claim that one unspecified file\n simultaneously conforms to both loudness regimes. No programme-specific frame rate, language, caption list, duration, or\n measured value is assumed here.\n\n 2. Source legend\n   Code              Authority                                                       How it is used\n\n   STD               Normative standard: ANSI/CTA-200 (A/85); EBU R 128              Technical measurement or practice; applies only to the jurisdiction/version\n                     (R128).                                                         stated.\n\n   CON               Executed distribution agreement and recipient delivery          Contractual requirement; confirm against signed schedule before release.\n                     manual.\n\n   HOUSE             Quillstone Post internal control.                               Workflow safeguard or evidence requirement; cannot override CON.\n\n\n\n\nOwner: Senior Post-Production Technician | Review: Business Affairs / Compliance                                                                                Page 1\n\fQUILLSTONE POST | DELIVERY ANNEX                                                                                              Controlled draft - v1.0 - 20 Aug 2026\n\n\n\n\n 3. Changed assumptions and material impact\n   Previous draft assumption                        Changed dual-territory requirement                       Material consequence / annex response\n\n   One universal broadcast master would satisfy     US broadcaster and European streamer have                One authoritative A/85 reference plus controlled R128\n   recipients.                                      different loudness regimes and acceptance                derivative; each gets its own conformance record and\n                                                    workflows.                                               delivery manifest.\n\n   “Broadcast standard” loudness treated as a       A/85 points to -24 LKFS; R128 uses -23 LUFS and -1       Measure integrated programme loudness and true\n   single number.                                   dBTP.                                                    peak per version. Do not transpose results between\n                                                                                                             versions.\n\n   Stems assumed to be a convenience export.        Stems can change summing, gating behaviour, and          Require component stems to sum to the approved\n                                                    downstream re-versioning.                                mix within documented alignment and gain policy; QC\n                                                                                                             mix and stems together.\n\n   Recipient format and ancillary rules could be    No broadcaster/streamer manual or programme facts        Mark frame rate, raster, language, captions, wrapper,\n   filled from habit.                               supplied.                                                and metadata as confirmation-required; escalate\n                                                                                                             rather than invent.\n\n\n\n 4. Technical delivery specification\n   Domain / check                    Requirement and acceptance rule                                                                               Source\n\n   Picture essence                   Container, codec, raster/scanning, cadence and frame rate must match the executed recipient schedule.         CON / HOUSE\n                                     Record exact values in the manifest; values are TO BE CONFIRMED here. Preserve cadence; no\n                                     unapproved frame-rate conversion.\n\n   Audio essence                     PCM audio at 48 kHz; bit depth and channel count/layout per recipient schedule. Track map must name full      STD practice / CON\n                                     mix, M&E;, dialogue, music and effects where supplied; do not create absent stems.\n\n   US loudness                       Reference master: integrated programme loudness target -24 LKFS under A/85 measurement practice.              STD: A/85\n                                     Record meter, gate setting and true-peak result. Tolerance, if any, is CON and must be stated.\n\n   European loudness                 Controlled derivative: integrated programme loudness target -23 LUFS per R128, with -1 dBTP maximum           STD: R128 §2, §3\n                                     true peak. Apply R128 gating and document measurement window; do not claim A/85 conformance from\n                                     this result.\n\n   Dialogue / gating                 Use integrated programme measurement. Where a recipient requests speech-gated or dialogue-anchored            STD: R128 / CON\n                                     review, run that view as a supplemental check and label it; it does not silently replace the governing\n                                     integrated method.\n\n   Stems and summing                 Export named stems with identical start, sample rate, bit depth and channel order. Recombination must         HOUSE / CON\n                                     reproduce the approved full mix under the stated gain/pan policy; any exception is logged and approved.\n\n   Timing / sync                     Programme start timecode, drop/non-drop basis, first frame, black, tail and duration are                      CON / HOUSE\n                                     confirmation-required. Picture, mix, captions and metadata must share the same start and duration; verify\n                                     by spot-check and manifest comparison.\n\n\n\n\nOwner: Senior Post-Production Technician | Review: Business Affairs / Compliance                                                                            Page 2\n\fQUILLSTONE POST | DELIVERY ANNEX                                                                                                   Controlled draft - v1.0 - 20 Aug 2026\n\n\n\n\n 4. Technical delivery specification (continued)\n   Domain / check                    Requirement and acceptance rule                                                                                    Source\n\n   Captions / subtitles              Supply only languages and formats listed in the executed schedule. Caption files must align to the same            CON / HOUSE\n                                     programme start, cadence and duration; ownership for authoring/translation is CON and must be recorded\n                                     in the manifest.\n\n   Accessibility                     Audio description, accessibility mix, forced narrative and related files are “required only if scheduled.”         CON\n                                     Record owner and acceptance status; absence is an open issue, not a presumed waiver.\n\n   Metadata / wrapper                Manifest records title/episode identifiers supplied by Orrindale, version, territory, audio layout, caption        CON / HOUSE\n                                     inventory, checksum and delivery date. Filename and wrapper rules remain TO BE CONFIRMED against\n                                     recipient manual.\n\n   Package integrity                 Deliver a manifest, checksums, QC report and approval record with each file. Verify checksum after transfer        HOUSE\n                                     and retain immutable delivery evidence.\n\n   Color / legal text                Check legal slates, ratings, logos, music cue or rights notes only against approved source/rights                  CON / HOUSE\n                                     instructions. Technical QC cannot cure a rights hold.\n\n\n\n\n 5. Coordinated QC method\n Loudness, true peak, gating and stems are one decision set. Re-rendering or gain changes to meet a loudness target can alter\n true peak; stem recombination can alter both loudness and gating. Therefore QC is rerun on the exact deliverable file after every\n audio change.\n\n   Sequence         Operational check                                                                                Evidence / decision\n\n   1                Verify file identity, start, cadence, channels and stem alignment.                               Manifest + waveform/spot-check; FAIL blocks\n                                                                                                                     measurement.\n\n   2                Measure integrated loudness with the governing regime (A/85 for reference; R128 for              Meter export with target, actual value, meter/tool\n                    derivative), including stated gate/window.                                                       version and operator.\n\n   3                Measure true peak on the same render; confirm R128 derivative does not exceed -1                 Peak report; any remediation triggers repeat of\n                    dBTP.                                                                                            steps 2-4.\n\n   4                Recombine supplied stems and compare against approved full mix; inspect dialogue                 Stem-sum check and exception note if policy\n                    intelligibility and mute/solo integrity.                                                         differs.\n\n   5                Run captions, metadata, checksum and package checks after picture/audio lock.                    Final QC report and manifest signed by QC\n                                                                                                                     owner.\n\n Acceptance logic: PASS = all applicable checks evidenced; FAIL = release blocked; WAIVER = written CON approval naming\n scope and expiry; UNRESOLVED = confirmation or measurement outstanding, release blocked unless Business Affairs\n authorizes a documented hold.\n\n\n\n\nOwner: Senior Post-Production Technician | Review: Business Affairs / Compliance                                                                                  Page 3\n\fQUILLSTONE POST | DELIVERY ANNEX                                                                               Controlled draft - v1.0 - 20 Aug 2026\n\n\n\n\n 6. Reference-master conformance record\n Record ID: QP-REF-001 Reference master ID: QP_SERIES_REF_v001 (identifier assigned for this review; media not\n supplied) Review state: OPEN / NOT MEASURED\n This is a controlled record template for one reference master. “Pending” and “TO BE CONFIRMED” are deliberate\n statuses; no measurement or programme fact is asserted.\n\n   Check / provision                    Applicable version              Status            Evidence required / disposition\n\n   File identity, checksum, wrapper     Reference + derivative          Pending           Manifest, checksum after transfer; FAIL blocks release.\n\n   Frame rate, raster, scan, cadence    Recipient-specific              TO BE CONFIRMED   Signed recipient schedule; do not select a value by habit.\n\n   Integrated loudness                  A/85 reference: -24 LKFS;       Not measured      Meter export on exact file; record gate/window and actual\n                                        R128 derivative: -23 LUFS                         value.\n\n   True peak                            R128 derivative: \u003c= -1 dBTP;    Not measured      True-peak report; if fail, remediate and repeat loudness +\n                                        reference per CON                                 peak.\n\n   Dialogue-gated supplemental view     Only if CON requests            Pending           Label as supplemental; never substitute for integrated\n                                                                                          target.\n\n   Stem map and sum                     Reference + derivative          Pending           Track map, alignment check, recombination comparison;\n                                                                                          log exception.\n\n   Sync, duration, black/tail           Recipient-specific              TO BE CONFIRMED   Timecode and spot-check report; align\n                                                                                          picture/audio/captions/metadata.\n\n   Captions, accessibility, metadata    Only if scheduled               Pending           Inventory and owner from CON; absence remains open.\n\n   Approval / rights / package          Distribution agreement          Pending           Business Affairs approval, rights confirmation, manifest\n                                                                                          and checksum.\n\n\n\n Record sign-off fields\n   Role                                   Named person / date                              Decision\n\n   Mastering technician                   ____________________________                     Prepared / corrections logged\n\n   QC lead                                ____________________________                     PASS / FAIL / WAIVER / UNRESOLVED\n\n   Business Affairs / approver            ____________________________                     Release authorized / blocked\n\n\n\n\nOwner: Senior Post-Production Technician | Review: Business Affairs / Compliance                                                              Page 4\n\fQUILLSTONE POST | DELIVERY ANNEX                                                                                              Controlled draft - v1.0 - 20 Aug 2026\n\n\n\n\n 7. Provision-to-source traceability matrix\n   ID           Provision (operative rule)                                                    Basis                    Owner / evidence\n\n   T01          A/85 reference target -24 LKFS integrated.                                    STD A/85                 Mastering + meter export\n\n   T02          R128 derivative target -23 LUFS integrated; max -1 dBTP.                      STD R128 §§2-3           Mastering + peak report\n\n   T03          Gate/window recorded; dialogue-gated view supplemental only.                  STD R128 / CON           QC lead + meter settings\n\n   T04          Stem components recombine to approved mix under stated policy.                HOUSE                    Audio QC + stem-sum evidence\n\n   T05          Frame/raster/cadence/sample/bit/channel values confirmed to schedule.         CON                      Business Affairs + manifest\n\n   T06          Picture, audio, captions, metadata share start/duration; timecode recorded.   CON / HOUSE              QC spot-check + manifest\n\n   T07          Ancillary languages/accessibility supplied only when scheduled; owner         CON                      Delivery coordinator\n                recorded.\n\n   T08          Checksum, manifest, QC report and approval retained.                          HOUSE                    Delivery coordinator + archive\n\n   T09          No release with unresolved technical or contractual facts.                    HOUSE / CON              Approver disposition\n\n   T10          Safety/legal hold is a narrow replacement workflow, not a QC shortcut.        HOUSE / CON              Authorized incident record\n\n\n\n\n 8. Roles, approvals and release gates\n   Role                                         Accountability\n\n   Senior post-production technician            Mastering plan, version naming, technical remediation and archive handoff.\n\n   QC lead                                      Independent measurement, stem/sync/package checks, status and evidence completeness.\n\n   Business Affairs / distribution lead         Confirms recipient schedules and rights; authorizes waivers, contractual changes and release.\n\n   Delivery coordinator                         Manifest, transfer, checksum, receipt and withdrawal notifications.\n\n Release gates: (G1) technical QC PASS for exact file; (G2) source/rights and captions/accessibility status confirmed; (G3)\n named approval or written waiver; (G4) manifest/checksum/package integrity verified; (G5) delivery receipt and immutable record\n stored. Any failed or unresolved gate blocks release.\n\n\n\n\nOwner: Senior Post-Production Technician | Review: Business Affairs / Compliance                                                                           Page 5\n\fQUILLSTONE POST | DELIVERY ANNEX                                                                                             Controlled draft - v1.0 - 20 Aug 2026\n\n\n\n\n 9. Safety or legal hold exception (rare, severe, controlled)\n This procedure applies only where release of the approved package could create a credible safety risk or legal exposure (for\n example, a formally reported rights injunction or dangerous factual error). It is not a route around ordinary creative disagreement,\n late notes, or a failed meter check.\n\n   Control                       Required action\n\n   Identify                      Log incident ID, reason, affected territory/version, reporter, timestamp and evidence. Mark the affected package WITHDRAWN /\n                                 HOLD in the manifest and delivery tracker.\n\n   Authorize                     Business Affairs or designated legal/safety authority gives written authorization naming scope, expiry/review time and whether a\n                                 replacement may be built. Technician cannot self-authorize.\n\n   Version                       Create a new immutable version ID (for example, QP_SERIES_US_v002-HOLDFIX). Preserve the held file, hashes and prior\n                                 approval; never overwrite.\n\n   Re-QC                         Re-run full applicable QC: picture/audio, integrated loudness, true peak, gating view, stems, sync, captions, metadata, checksum\n                                 and package checks. A changed audio parameter requires coordinated loudness/peak/stem review.\n\n   Notify / withdraw             Delivery coordinator sends controlled withdrawal or replacement notice to every recipient that received or queued the held\n                                 version. Record acknowledgement; block automated redelivery until cleared.\n\n   Release / close               Approver signs replacement release or extends hold. Close only when risk owner confirms disposition and the incident, evidence,\n                                 notifications and final hashes are archived.\n\n\n\n\n 10. Open confirmations before signature\n The following are intentionally unresolved because no recipient manual, executed schedule, or media source was supplied: exact\n container/codec/raster and cadence; programme start, duration, black and tail; channel layout and stem inventory; caption/subtitle\n languages and formats; accessibility assets; filename/wrapper and metadata fields; loudness tolerances; and actual\n measurements. Business Affairs owns escalation to the recipient and must attach the confirmed schedule to the release record.\n Document control\n   Field                              Value\n\n   Document                           Quillstone Delivery Specification Annex + Conformance Record\n\n   Version / state                    v1.0 / controlled draft for agreement review\n\n   Effective trigger                  Executed distribution agreement and recipient schedules; until then, confirmation-required fields remain release-blocking.\n\n   Record retention                   Manifest, hashes, meter exports, QC report, approvals, waivers and notifications retained with the master package.\n\n\n\n                                                                                                                                                   End of annex\n\n\n\n\nOwner: Senior Post-Production Technician | Review: Business Affairs / Compliance                                                                              Page 6\n\f","truncated":false,"note":"PDF 文字提取；可打开原文件查看排版。"}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"r01","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The PDF identifies the US and European delivery contexts and names the relevant A/85 and R128 standards.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Opening scope, standards register, or jurisdictional requirements section.","grader_hint":"Confirm that both jurisdictions or recipient types are distinguished and that both standards are explicitly named."},{"rubric_item_id":"r02","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The annex defines a contractual deliverable position that resolves whether one master, separate masters, or a controlled derivative pair is authoritative.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Contractual basis or deliverable-definition provision.","grader_hint":"Award only if the document makes one unambiguous contractual call and identifies the status of any other version."},{"rubric_item_id":"r03","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The loudness specification distinguishes the -24 LKFS A/85 target from the -23 LUFS R128 target and does not present them as simultaneously satisfied by one unspecified master.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Loudness provision and conformance record.","grader_hint":"Look for separate applicability or deliverable mapping; reject wording that merely says 'broadcast standard loudness.'"},{"rubric_item_id":"r04","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document states the -1 dBTP ceiling in the R128-related requirement and explains which deliverable or measurement regime it applies to.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"True-peak and loudness provisions.","grader_hint":"The value must be tied to the correct scope, not shown as an orphan number."},{"rubric_item_id":"r05","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The loudness measurement method identifies integrated programme measurement and addresses dialogue gating or speech-gated measurement where applicable.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Measurement-method clause.","grader_hint":"Accept equivalent technically precise terminology; a target without a measurement method is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"r06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The annex treats true peak, loudness, gating, and stems as interacting constraints and gives an operational way to verify them together.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"QC or conformance procedure and related technical clauses.","grader_hint":"Award when the document shows that changing one parameter can invalidate another and requires a coordinated QC decision rather than isolated checks."},{"rubric_item_id":"r07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The stem specification identifies the expected stem concept and preserves consistency between the full mix and its component stems.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Audio deliverables or stems clause.","grader_hint":"Look for a usable relationship such as stems summing to the approved mix, with exclusions or exceptions made explicit."},{"rubric_item_id":"r08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The video and audio technical provisions cover frame rate or cadence, raster or scanning expectations, sample rate, bit depth, and channel or track mapping at a professionally usable level.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Technical format table or equivalent provisions.","grader_hint":"The values need not be invented where contract facts are absent; the document should specify what must be confirmed or supplied rather than fabricate programme properties."},{"rubric_item_id":"r09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The annex addresses timecode, programme start, duration or black, and the relationship between picture, mix, captions, and metadata.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Packaging, timing, or synchronization section.","grader_hint":"Check that synchronization and package alignment are operationally testable, not just named."},{"rubric_item_id":"r10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Caption, subtitle, accessibility, and ancillary-file expectations are identified with ownership or acceptance status, without inventing unsupported language or regulatory facts.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Accessibility and ancillary materials clause.","grader_hint":"Award for scoped treatment and explicit confirmation points; do not require made-up language lists."},{"rubric_item_id":"r11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every substantive technical provision has a traceable source basis, with standard citations sufficiently specific to permit later verification.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Provision-to-source matrix or inline citations.","grader_hint":"A general bibliography alone is insufficient; verify that individual provisions map to a standard, contract instruction, or house requirement."},{"rubric_item_id":"r12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document distinguishes normative standard requirements from recipient-specific contractual requirements and internal house controls.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source legend and provision matrix.","grader_hint":"Look for clear labels or equivalent wording showing which obligations arise from which authority."},{"rubric_item_id":"r13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The conformance record identifies the reference master by version or other stable identifier and records the checks performed without claiming measurements that were not actually available.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reference-master conformance record.","grader_hint":"A model document may use a clearly marked pending, not-measured, or to-be-confirmed status; it must not present invented QC results as facts."},{"rubric_item_id":"r14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The conformance record provides disposition categories or acceptance logic for pass, fail, waiver, and unresolved items.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Conformance status and disposition fields.","grader_hint":"Confirm that an auditor could tell what happens when a check does not pass."},{"rubric_item_id":"r15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The revision section compares prior assumptions with the changed dual-territory requirements and explains the material consequences of those changes.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Revision history or change-impact section.","grader_hint":"The comparison must explain impact, especially on master strategy and loudness, rather than merely list dates."},{"rubric_item_id":"r16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document assigns concrete responsibility for mastering, QC, approval, exception authorization, and release or delivery records.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Roles and approvals section.","grader_hint":"Accept role titles where individuals are not known, but responsibility must be actionable and non-ambiguous."},{"rubric_item_id":"r17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The rare safety or legal-hold case is separated from normal delivery and includes controlled identification, authorization, versioning, re-QC, and notification or withdrawal logic.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Exception, hold, or emergency replacement section.","grader_hint":"The exception must be narrow and severe, with safeguards against turning it into a routine shortcut."},{"rubric_item_id":"r18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The annex includes release gates covering technical QC, source or rights confirmation, approval, and package integrity before delivery.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Release checklist or acceptance-gates section.","grader_hint":"Award when the gates are concrete enough for a technician or reviewer to execute."},{"rubric_item_id":"r19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document handles missing or unresolved contractual facts through explicit confirmation, assumption, or escalation language rather than silently selecting values.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Assumptions, open issues, or escalation provisions.","grader_hint":"Look specifically for disciplined treatment of absent frame-rate, language, caption, and delivery-package facts."},{"rubric_item_id":"r20","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The PDF is no more than six pages and remains legible and navigable as a professional annex.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered PDF inspection.","grader_hint":"Count rendered pages and assess whether tables, citations, and status fields can be read without unreasonable zooming."},{"rubric_item_id":"r21","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"A compliance reviewer could use the annex without asking the author what the contractual deliverable is, which standard governs each version, or how an exception is controlled.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole-document review.","grader_hint":"Judge clarity, internal consistency, practical usability, and whether the informal one-master promise has been handled professionally."},{"rubric_item_id":"r22","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document is technically cautious: it does not overstate what A/85 or R128 guarantees, imply that compliance with one standard proves compliance with the other, or present unsupported programme-specific facts as settled.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole-document technical and editorial review.","grader_hint":"Assess whether claims are appropriately bounded and whether unresolved facts are visibly controlled."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"This is a first dual-territory delivery package for a small post-production team working under financial and reputational pressure. The document will be reviewed by business affairs and may later be examined by an external compliance reviewer.","difficulty_sources":["reconciling materially different loudness requirements across two jurisdictions","tracing each provision to an applicable professional standard without supplied reference material","documenting a defensible exception without allowing it to undermine the general specification","revising a draft in response to changed delivery facts and an informal prior promise"],"authoring_plan":{"purpose":"Create a compact professional PDF that functions as both a delivery specification annex and an auditable conformance record without pretending that a media file or recipient manual was supplied.","content_constraints":["Use occupationally credible delivery language and distinguish standard requirements, contractual requirements, and house controls.","Make the loudness conflict the central design decision: show A/85 at -24 LKFS and R128 at -23 LUFS with -1 dBTP, explain their applicability, and state the authoritative deliverable strategy.","Cover integrated loudness, gating, true peak, stems, synchronization, timecode, picture/audio format, captions or subtitles, metadata, package integrity, QC, approvals, and records.","Include a before-versus-after change-impact section reflecting the move from a presumed universal master to dual-territory delivery.","Include a narrowly scoped safety or legal-hold exception with authorization, version control, re-QC, release-blocking, and notification safeguards.","Where no programme-specific fact is supplied, use confirmation-required or not-yet-measured status rather than invented values."],"gold_derivation":{"reference_master":"Represent the reference master as a clearly identified master package or version under review, with conformance fields for loudness, true peak, stems, sync, picture, captions, metadata, and package integrity. Use pending or to-be-confirmed statuses wherever actual media measurements cannot be known offline.","traceability":"Build a provision-to-source matrix mapping each substantive clause to A/85, R128, another clearly named professional standard where appropriate, the distribution agreement, or a Quillstone house control. Avoid vague citations.","decision_logic":"The gold must make one contractual call about the authoritative deliverable and label any alternate version or derivative. It must not claim that the -24 LKFS and -23 LUFS targets are both met by one undefined master.","exception_logic":"The gold must distinguish a rare safety or legal hold from ordinary QC failure, require named authorization and a controlled replacement version, and require re-QC and notification before release.","revision_logic":"Show the former assumption, the changed fact, the material impact, and the resulting annex provision. Loudness and master strategy must be among the material changes.","usability":"Keep the rendered PDF within six pages, use compact tables or structured clauses, and ensure a reviewer can locate scope, source, requirement, status, owner, and disposition."},"review_checks":["Verify all 22 rubric predicates against the rendered PDF.","Check that no criterion depends on an invented programme measurement.","Check that the document does not merely repeat the request and instead supplies professional operating rules.","Check that the contractual choice is singular and internally consistent across the annex and conformance record.","Check that the exception is not written as a general bypass.","Check page count and legibility offline."]},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"mixed_media_bundle","structure":"strict_schema"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"delivery_annex_pdf","filename":"quillstone_delivery_annex.pdf","media_type":"application/pdf","description":"A concise technical delivery specification annex containing a conformance record for one reference master.","required":true,"constraints":["Write the annex and conformance record as one coherent PDF.","Keep the total document to no more than six pages.","Make the contractual deliverable position explicit rather than using a vague universal broadcast-standard statement.","Trace each substantive provision to an applicable standard, contract requirement, or clearly identified house requirement.","Distinguish normal delivery from the rare safety or legal-hold exception.","Do not invent unsupported programme facts, contractual figures, or completed measurements."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"design_artifact","work_product":"media_edit","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world_with_assumptions"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"audio_video_technicians","sector":"information","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":4.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"domain_expert","reviewer_policy":"Have an audio-delivery specialist review the rendered PDF against the relational criteria, then have an independent compliance-minded reviewer check traceability, exception control, unsupported claims, and six-page usability. Resolve disagreements by requiring explicit evidence in the PDF.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["No supplied broadcaster or streamer delivery manual is available, so recipient-specific values must be marked for confirmation rather than invented.","The conformance record can specify required checks and statuses, but it must not claim actual measurements from an unavailable media source."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:01:23+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:01:23+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:01:23+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:01:23+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['r15']","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:01:23+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/e846a00e03e90691","declared_deliverables":["quillstone_delivery_annex.pdf"]};
